---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, POLICY_UPDATED } from "../lib/site";

/* Describes what the site actually does. Every claim here is checkable
   against the code: there is no analytics script, no tag manager, no
   advertising pixel and no cookie set anywhere in the project. If that ever
   changes, this page changes in the same commit. */
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy — OLMIKAYA"
  description="What OLMIKAYA collects, what it does not, and how to get it removed."
  current="privacy"
  showSections={false}
>
  <section class="section--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="col-8 start-3 stack reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
          <h1 class="display-l">Privacy policy</h1>
          <p class="lead">
            The short version: the only thing we ever ask for is an email
            address, and only if you want the letter. Nothing else is collected,
            and nothing is sold.
          </p>
          <p class="small muted">Last updated {POLICY_UPDATED}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="col-8 start-3">
          <div class="prose reveal">
            <h2>What we collect</h2>
            <p>
              <strong>Your email address, if you give it to us.</strong> The
              sign-up form for the letter is the only place this site asks for
              anything. We store the address, the date you signed up and which
              page you signed up from. That is the whole record.
            </p>
            <p>
              We do not ask for your name, and there is nowhere on this site to
              create an account, because there are no accounts.
            </p>

            <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
            <p>
              There is no analytics on this site. No Google Analytics, no tag
              manager, no advertising pixel, no session recording, no
              fingerprinting and no third-party script of any kind. We cannot
              tell you how many people read a given piece, because we do not
              measure it.
            </p>
            <p>
              The typefaces are served from this site rather than from Google
              Fonts, so reading a page does not tell Google that you did.
            </p>

            <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
            <p>
              <strong>This site sets no cookies.</strong> That is why there is
              no cookie banner — there is nothing to consent to.
            </p>
            <p>
              One thing is stored in your browser: when you sign up to the
              letter, the site leaves a note to itself so that it stops showing
              you the sign-up form. It records only that this browser signed up
              and whether the address was confirmed. It holds no email address,
              it is never sent anywhere, and clearing your browser data removes
              it. Every sign-up panel carries a control that clears it too.
            </p>

            <h2>Who else handles your address</h2>
            <p>
              <strong>Kit</strong> runs the mailing list and sends the letter.
              Your address is stored on their systems, in the United States,
              under their own privacy policy. They are a processor acting on our
              instructions and do not use your address for their own purposes.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the site and, like any web host,
              processes the requests your browser makes in order to serve pages
              and to block abuse.
            </p>
            <p>
              Nobody else. We do not sell, rent, share or trade your address,
              and we do not hand it to anyone buying an audience.
            </p>

            <h2>Confirming, and leaving</h2>
            <p>
              Signing up is double opt-in: you are not added to the mailing list
              until you click the link in the confirmation email. Sign up and
              never confirm, and you are never sent anything.
            </p>
            <p>
              Every issue carries an unsubscribe link at the foot. It works on
              the first click and needs no email to us and no reason given.
            </p>

            <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
            <p>
              Until you unsubscribe, or until you ask us to delete it. We do not
              keep a shadow copy of people who have left beyond what Kit retains
              to honour an unsubscribe.
            </p>

            <h2>Your rights</h2>
            <p>
              You can ask what we hold about you, ask for it corrected, ask for
              it deleted, or ask for a copy. Write to{" "}
              <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and we
              will act on it. Since the record is one email address and a date,
              this is usually a very short conversation.
            </p>
            <p>
              We are based in Kenya and operate under the Data Protection Act
              2019. If you are in a jurisdiction with its own rules, those
              rights apply too and we will honour them.
            </p>

            <h2>Children</h2>
            <p>
              This site is not aimed at children and we do not knowingly collect
              anything from them.
            </p>

            <h2>Changes</h2>
            <p>
              If this policy changes in substance, the date at the top changes
              with it. We will not quietly broaden what we collect.
            </p>

            <h2>Contact</h2>
            <p>
              <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
